[
    {
        "content": "<p>Is the following good code style? (<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Algebra/Operations.html#Submodule.prod_span\">Submodule.prod_span</a>)</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">prod_span</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∏</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">span</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">span</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∏</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Classical</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">decEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">induction_on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">one_eq_span</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">singleton_one</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod_insert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod_insert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">span_mul_span</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I.e. via <code>let := Classical.decEq ι</code> the proof is using results from the <code>Classical</code> namespace without opening it. Replacing that line with <code>classical</code> would not break the proof.</p>\n<p>This (more precisely the regex pattern <code>Classical\\.[^(choose)]</code>) appears around 950 times in mathlib. I think it would be preferable to replace these with the much more common <code>classical / open (scoped) Classical</code> (place it at the front of the proof that is), as it signals more clearly when classical logic is needed.</p>\n<p>Would that be better?</p>",
        "id": 612851641,
        "sender_full_name": "Felix Pernegger",
        "timestamp": 1785095284
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>surely here it would be better to use <code>induction</code> with <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.cons_induction_on#doc\">docs#Finset.cons_induction_on</a></p>",
        "id": 612851922,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1785095550
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe, but we definitely can't use <code>induction</code> for all 950 appearances :)</p>",
        "id": 612851972,
        "sender_full_name": "Felix Pernegger",
        "timestamp": 1785095622
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>like this</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pointwise</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">prod_span</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∏</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">span</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">span</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∏</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">induction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cons_induction_on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">empty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">one_eq_span</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">singleton_one</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod_cons</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod_cons</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">span_mul_span</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 612852064,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1785095756
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would expect many uses of <code>classical</code> are from using <code>Finset.induction_on</code> instead of <code>Finset.cons_induction_on</code></p>",
        "id": 612852099,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1785095802
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"780789\">Felix Pernegger</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Using.20.60Classical.60.20but.20not.20opening.20it/near/612851641\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I.e. via <code>let := Classical.decEq ι</code> the proof is using results from the <code>Classical</code> namespace without opening it. Replacing that line with <code>classical</code> would not break the proof.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>In general though the <code>let</code> may work in places where <code>classical</code> may not, since the latter enables the instance for all types not just one type.</p>",
        "id": 612854991,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1785098077
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My inclination would be to leave this to the author, and encourage <code>classical</code> if there are say &gt;2 such lets</p>",
